            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical analysis of acute invasive fungal sinusitis with orbital infection].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1528-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical manifestation of acute invasive fungal sinusitis was associated with facial pain,altered sense of smell, blindness and headache. Physical examinations show that dark brown nasal secretions with bone resorption in paranasal sinus. Radiographi parameters showed uneven density in paranasal sinus and intraorbital extension. Fungus smears and pathological examination can make a definitive diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
